r":"1"}],"thesis":"A **blockbuster Q3 driven almost entirely by product cracks**, not crude advantage. EBITDA more than doubled YoY (INR 2,824 cr vs 1,064 cr) as diesel/ATF/MS cracks spiked (HSD ~$15→$21, MS ~$8→$13) amid sanctions-driven market dislocation — more than offsetting the loss of (small, \"opportunity\") Russian barrels, which MRPL has now fully exited. Best-ever energy efficiency (MBN 67) and fuel-&-loss (10.06%), net debt down to ~INR 9,290 cr (D/E 0.63). Mgmt is candid that the Q3 GRM spike is **not sustainable** — current cracks have already moderated back to ~$14–15 (Q2 levels). The real structural story management is selling is the **pivot from a pure base refinery to a refining-plus-marketing business**: own retail outlets 200 → 250 (FY26-end) → 500 (3yr) → 1,000 (5yr), to capture higher, more stable margins than volatile exports.","trig":[]},"lm":"","m":31047,"mem":0,"pdd":"","prev_stage":2,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":null,"s":"MRPL","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"162.6","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"17.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"-0.3","vpe_zone_cumul_df":"-0.3"},"t":""}},"s":"MRPL"}